course: dictionary
lesson: 10370
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word tread can be a verb or a noun, so it can mean different things. When you meet it, look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Snakes bite people mostly when they are trodden on, grabbed or cornered.» Trodden is a form of tread, so it must mean stepped on, because snakes bite when someone steps on them.
explain: Tread can also be a noun, a thing you can name. «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away so the rubber can grip.» The clues are grooves, water and grip, so here tread means the pattern on the outside of a tyre that grips the road.
explain: Some tread phrases have their own meanings. «Tread water» means to stay upright in water by moving your legs and arms, without swimming forward. «Tread carefully» means to move with caution, so you are careful about where you put your feet.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «stepped on» in place of «trodden on» and «pattern on the tyre» in place of «tread», and see if each one still makes sense.
fact: Tread can be a verb (to walk or step on something) or a noun (a way of walking, a pattern on a tyre, or the flat part of a step).
fact: «A heavy tread» means the sound or way someone walks.
fact: Tyre tread is the pattern of grooves that grips the road; the UK minimum tread depth for cars is 1.6 millimetres.
fact: A layer of water between tyres and road can make a car skid; this is called aquaplaning, and tread pushes the water away.
fact: «Tread on someone's toes» is a phrase that means to upset someone or treat them unfairly. You will see it in stories, not in the middle of a swimming pool.
exercise: «Snakes bite people mostly when they are trodden on, grabbed or cornered.» What does trodden on mean here? | *Stepped on | Cooked in a pan | Put in a box | Kissed gently
exercise: «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away so the rubber can grip.» What is the tread on a tyre? | *The pattern of grooves that grips the road | The steel cords inside | The colour of the car | The rubber smell
exercise: In swimming lessons pupils learn to «tread water». What does tread water mean? | *Stay upright by moving your legs and arms, without swimming forward | Walk fast across the pool | Dive to the bottom | Splash loudly
test: «A heavy tread» on the stairs is the sound someone makes when they walk. What does tread mean in «a heavy tread»? | *The sound or way someone walks | To press something flat | A pattern on a shoe | The flat part of a step
test: Dad says, «Tread carefully on the ice.» What does he mean? | Wear your best shoes | Run as fast as you can | Sing a loud song | *Move with care
exam: Which sentence uses tread as a noun? | Snakes bite people when they are trodden on | Tread water to stay safe in the pool | Tread carefully on the ice | *The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away
